Z||000001||jlhuber||01-26-2000||10:26 PM||||my cousin owns a scuba/kayak/gear store named Dive And Glide in Bay City, Michigan.  he scubas where ever he can when ever he gets a chance to go.  he started teaching me but i joined the military (stupid mistake) before we were finished.  i loved the little bit that i did do, and hope to finish the school and get certified when i get out of active duty in april of 2001.  i am also working on getting my private pilots license so that i can fly myself to vacation spots.  anyway, thats my $.02 worth||||reg||14
Z||000002||Monkeyman||01-27-2000||04:52 AM||||I used to until I drowned one day and died.  It's tough to swim when you're dead.<P>Seriously though, I haven't in about 10 years.  Used to be PADI, but have long since lost my cert.  I keep meaning to get into it again, but I just don't have the time or money.  I sold all of my equipment (I might have my snorkel and flippers around here somewhere mildewing!).||||reg||1
Z||000003||fierosound||01-27-2000||11:32 PM||||I spent 5 months in the Philippines (extended holiday) in 1999, and travelled around the country.  Great snorkling/diving sites in many areas.  <P>There's a diving paradise in Sabang Beach - I'm not a diver, but had done alot of snorkling there during the month I was there.  I had planned to look into a diving course when I had to cut my visit short after taking a bad fall from a banca (outrigger) and braking my heelbone.<P>I plan to get back there again in 2001 for several months.  Have a look at my Philippines website at:<P> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/adventureman99_1999" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/adventureman99_1999</A> <p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 01-27-2000).]||||reg||10
